<newsitem itemid="640051" id="root" date="1997-06-05" xml:lang="en">
<title>USA: Top manufacturing countries - survey.</title>
<headline>Top manufacturing countries - survey.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following are the countries with the most major manufacturing companies in 1996, according to IndustryWeek magazine's IndustryWeek 1000 list, compiled with Dun &amp; Bradstreet Corp. and Moody's Investor Service:</p>
<p>United States - 329 companies</p>
<p>Japan - 221</p>
<p>Britain - 84</p>
<p>Germany - 51</p>
<p>France - 50</p>
<p>Canada - 32</p>
<p>Sweden - 23</p>
<p>Italy - 21</p>
<p>South Korea - 19</p>
<p>Australia - 19</p>
<p>Netherlands - 16</p>
<p>Switzerland - 15</p>
<p>South Africa - 15</p>
<p>Finland - 14</p>
<p>Brazil - 11</p>
<p>Belgium - 9</p>
<p>India - 8</p>
<p>Mexico - 8</p>
<p>Spain - 7</p>
<p>Taiwan - 7</p>
<p>Norway - 7</p>
</text>
